		{"id":"risk","type":"text","text":"## Risk Analysis (FMEA)\n\n### Critical Risks (RPN>125)\n| Failure | RPN | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| EMI/EMC | 140 | Ferrite chokes, STP CAN |\n| AI inference fail | 126 | Watchdog, fallback spray |\n\n### High Risks (100-125)\n| Failure | RPN | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Motor failure | 108 | SMF handler, 6-motor |\n| ESC failure | 108 | Individual ESCs, fuses |\n| Battery thermal | 100 | BMS, thermal cutoff |\n| Pre-charge fail | 120 | Thermal fuse |\n| Busbar overheat | 108 | Upgrade 20×5mm |\n| Wire chafing | 128 | Silicone, grommets |\n\n### Failsafe Actions\n| Trigger | Action |\n|---|---|\n| RC loss (>1.5s) | RTL |\n| Battery <42V | Stop spray, land |\n| Battery <39.6V | Immediate land |\n| GPS loss (>3s) | Hover → Land |\n| Telemetry loss | Continue auto |\n| Jetson fail | Stop spray, fly |\n| Motor failure | SMF → land |\n\n### Environmental Limits\n| Condition | Limit |\n|---|---|\n| Temperature | -20°C to 50°C |\n| Wind | <5m/s spray |\n| Altitude | <1000m ASL |\n| Rain | Prohibited |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot Failsafe docs — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":-560,"y":800,"width":480,"height":1100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"maintenance","type":"text","text":"## Preventive Maintenance\n\n### Pre-Flight (Every Flight)\n- [ ] Battery charge (no swelling)\n- [ ] Prop tightness\n- [ ] GPS lock (10+ sats)\n- [ ] Radio link test\n- [ ] Frame inspection\n- [ ] Nozzle clear\n\n### Every 10 Flights\n- [ ] Motor bearing inspection\n- [ ] ESC connector check\n- [ ] Wiring inspection\n- [ ] Compass recalibration\n\n### Every 50 Flights\n- [ ] Prop replacement\n- [ ] Motor bearing replacement\n- [ ] Arm bolt retorque\n- [ ] Full PID re-tune\n- [ ] Battery capacity test\n\n### Every 100 Flights\n- [ ] Full teardown\n- [ ] Frame crack check\n- [ ] ESC/FC firmware update\n- [ ] Battery retirement check\n\n### Component Lifespan\n| Component | Life | Warning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Props | 50 flights | Chips |\n| Motors | 500 hours | Noise |\n| ESCs | 1000 hours | Erratic |\n| Battery | 300 cycles | <80% cap |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot maintenance — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":-2360,"y":1240,"width":480,"height":1040,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"data-logging","type":"text","text":"## Data Logging Architecture\n\n### Log Sources\n| Source | Rate | Format |\n|---|---|---|\n| ArduPilot .bin | 10Hz | Binary |\n| GPS Position | 5Hz | Binary |\n| IMU Data | 100Hz | Binary |\n| AI Decisions | Per-frame | JSON |\n| Spray Events | Per-event | JSON |\n\n### AI Decision JSON Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp_ms\": 1234567890,\n  \"frame_id\": 4521,\n  \"gps\": {\"lat\": 18.52, \"lon\": 73.85},\n  \"ndvi\": 0.35,\n  \"classification\": \"moderate_stress\",\n  \"spray_rate_lpha\": 100,\n  \"inference_ms\": 87,\n  \"model_version\": \"v1.2.0\"\n}\n```\n\n### Storage & Retention\n| Log Type | Retention |\n|---|---|\n| Flight .bin | 30 days |\n| AI decisions | 90 days |\n| Spray events | 1 year |\n| Mission summaries | Permanent |\n\n### Security\n- AES-256-GCM encryption\n- TLS 1.3 in transit\n- TPM 2.0 secure boot\n- HMAC-SHA256 signatures","x":1600,"y":-775,"width":480,"height":975,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"build","type":"text","text":"## Build & Test Sequence\n\n### Build Order (20 Steps)\n**Phase 1 — Assembly:**\n1. Frame Assembly (threadlocker)\n2. Motor Mounting (6× CW/CCW)\n3. ESC Installation (150A fuses)\n4. Power Distribution (busbar)\n5. FC + GPS Mounting (damped)\n6. Wiring Harness (8/14/20 AWG)\n\n**Phase 2 — Bench Testing:**\n7. Smoke Stopper Test\n8. ESC Calibration\n9. Compass Calibration\n10. Radio Calibration\n11. Flight Mode Config\n12. Failsafe Config\n\n**Phase 3 — Ground Testing:**\n13. Ground Sweep (no props)\n14. Prop Balancing\n15. Tethered Hover (5m tether)\n\n**Phase 4 — Flight Testing:**\n16. Free Hover (1-2m)\n17. Mode Testing (Stab→Loiter→RTL)\n18. Flight Envelope\n19. Spray Integration\n20. Mission Waypoint Testing\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot build guides — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":1360,"y":1750,"width":480,"height":850,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"alt-batteries","type":"text","text":"## Alternative Batteries\n\n### Tattu Pro 12S 22Ah (25C)\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Capacity | 22,000mAh |\n| Energy | 976.8Wh |\n| Weight | 6,300g |\n| C-Rating | 25C |\n| Price | ₹37,897 |\n| Source | Mavdrones |\n\n### GenX 12S 22Ah (Budget)\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Capacity | 22,000mAh |\n| Energy | 1003.2Wh |\n| Weight | 4,888g |\n| Price | ₹24,170 |\n| Source | Robokits |\n\n### Comparison at 4.9kg weight\n| Type | Capacity | Energy | Endurance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tattu 30Ah | 30Ah | 1,332 Wh | 28 min |\n| Tattu 22Ah | 22Ah | 977 Wh | 21 min |\n| GenX 22Ah | 22Ah | 1,003 Wh | 21 min |\n\n### Verdict\n- **30Ah (current)**: Best endurance\n- **22Ah Pro**: Smart BMS, data logging\n- **GenX 22Ah**: Budget, same performance\n\n**Source:** Tattu — https://genstattu.com\nMavdrones — https://mavdrones.com\nRobokits — https://robokits.co.in","x":-4360,"y":-1550,"width":620,"height":950,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"alt-frames","type":"text","text":"## Alternative Frames\n\n### Tarot T960\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wheelbase | 960mm |\n| Weight | 1,050g |\n| Payload | 2-3.5 kg |\n| Tube | 25mm |\n| Price | ₹29,565 |\n| Source | RC Mumbai |\n| **Issue** | Too small for 16L |\n\n### DJI M600 Clone\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wheelbase | 1,600mm |\n| Weight | 7.2 kg |\n| Arms | Quick-release |\n| Price | ₹22,000+ |\n| **Issue** | Heavier, no folding |\n\n### EFT E616P (Selected)\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wheelbase | 1,648mm |\n| Weight | 7.5 kg |\n| Max MTOW | 35 kg |\n| Tank | 16L built-in |\n| Price | ₹52,780 |\n| **Why** | Tank integrated, proven |\n\n**Source:** Tarot — https://www.tarotrc.com\nRC Mumbai — https://rcmumbai.com","x":-4360,"y":-540,"width":700,"height":960,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"data-pipeline","type":"text","text":"## Data Pipeline\n\n### Real-Time Path (On-Device)\n```\nCamera → Jetson Orin\n  → NDVI compute (2ms)\n  → YOLO classify (12ms)\n  → Spray decision (1ms)\n  → MAVLink cmd (5ms)\n  → Pump actuation (100ms)\n  Total: ~120ms latency\n```\n\n### Post-Flight Path\n```\nFlight logs → Laptop\n  → Mission Planner export\n  → NDVI GeoTIFF generation\n  → Crop health map\n  → Prescription map\n  → Next mission planning\n```\n\n### Storage Architecture\n| Location | Data | Retention |\n|---|---|---|\n| Jetson SSD 512GB | Video, AI logs | 30 days |\n| SD 128GB | .bin logs | 30 days |\n| Laptop | NDVI maps | 1 year |\n| Cloud | Aggregated | Permanent |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot logging — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":2120,"y":-1600,"width":480,"height":825,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"alt-motors","type":"text","text":"## Alternative Motors\n\n### T-Motor U13 II KV130\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| KV | 130 |\n| Thrust | 24.3 kg |\n| Weight | 990g |\n| Price | ₹42,539 |\n| Source | MG Super Labs |\n\n### MAD Agriculture Motors\n| Model | Price | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| M10 | $267 | IPE agriculture |\n| M17 | $326 | IPE agriculture |\n| M30 | $629 | IPE agriculture |\n| 8318 IPE | $198 | Budget option |\n\n### Decision Matrix\n| Factor | X9 G2L | T-Motor U13 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Thrust | 24 kg | 24.3 kg |\n| Weight | 1,532g | 990g |\n| Price | ₹16,250 | ₹42,539 |\n| Proven | Yes | Yes |\n| **Verdict** | **Best value** | Performance |\n\n**Source:** T-Motor — https://store.tmotor.com\nMAD Components — https://www.madcomponents.com","x":-4360,"y":-2400,"width":620,"height":820,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"power-dist","type":"text","text":"## Power Distribution\n\n### Busbar System\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Type | Copper Busbar |\n| Dimensions | 15×5mm (75mm²) |\n| Max Current | 200A+ continuous |\n| Main Fuse | 300A MEGA |\n| ESC Fuses | 6× 150A MEGA |\n| Connectors | AS150U (battery) |\n| **AS150 Price** | **₹537-1,595** |\n\n### Wire Sizing\n| Circuit | Current | Gauge |\n|---|---|---|\n| Battery→PDB | 136A max | 8 AWG |\n| PDB→ESC | 25A each | 14 AWG |\n| 5V rail | 5A | 20 AWG |\n| Signal | <1A | 26 AWG |\n\n### ⚠️ Pre-Charge Circuit (MANDATORY)\n- 12S (>44V) → 5,040A inrush!\n- With 110Ω (2×parallel): 0.4A ✅\n- τ = 150ms, 95% in 450ms\n- BOM: ₹800-2,000\n\n**Source:** RC Mumbai — https://rcmumbai.com\nAS150: Robu.in — https://robu.in","x":-1000,"y":-2480,"width":480,"height":840,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"frame","type":"text","text":"## Frame — EFT E616P\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wheelbase | 1,648mm |\n| Material | T700 Carbon Fiber |\n| Frame Weight | 7.5 kg |\n| Max MTOW | 35 kg (stock) |\n| Tank | 16L HDPE belly |\n| Folded | 1102×970×600mm |\n| Expanded | 2428×2428×600mm |\n| **Price** | **₹52,780** |\n| **Source** | Robokits India |\n\n### Structural Analysis\n- Arm: 25mm OD × 2mm wall (6061-T6)\n- 3g maneuver stress: 23.3 MPa\n- Safety Factor (3g): **10.3** ✅\n- Safety Factor (6g): **5.2** ✅\n\n### ⚠️ Resonance Risk\n- 25mm arm natural freq: 32 Hz\n- Motor shaft freq at hover: 32-36 Hz\n- **OVERLAP → Resonance risk**\n- **FIX: Upgrade to 30mm arm (48 Hz)**\n\n**Source:** Robokits India — https://robokits.co.in\nUAVGarage — https://uavgarage.com","x":-2600,"y":-3200,"width":480,"height":750,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"fc","type":"text","text":"## Flight Controller — Pixhawk 6C\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Processor | STM32H743 480MHz |\n| IMU | Dual (ICM-42688+BMI088) |\n| Barometer | MS5611 |\n| Mag | IST8310 |\n| GPS Ports | 2× UART |\n| CAN Ports | 2× |\n| PWM Outputs | 8 |\n| Firmware | ArduCopter 4.4 |\n| Weight | 59.3g (aluminum) |\n| **Price** | **₹26,749** |\n| **Source** | Indian Robo Store |\n\n### Port Allocation\n| Port | Device | Protocol | Baud |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| UART1 | GPS 1 M10 | UBX Binary | 115200 |\n| UART2 | GPS 2 M10 | UBX Binary | 115200 |\n| UART3 | RFD868x | MAVLink | 115200 |\n| UART6 | ELRS RX | CRSF | 420000 |\n| CAN1 | Jetson Orin | CAN | 1 Mbps |\n| PWM CH5 | Pump | PWM 50Hz | — |\n\n### PID Starting Points\n- ATC_RAT_RLL_P=0.15 I=0.10 D=0.005\n- ATC_RAT_PIT_P=0.15 I=0.10 D=0.005\n- ATC_RAT_YAW_P=0.20 I=0.02\n- MOT_THST_HOVER=0.45\n\n**Source:** Indian Robo Store — https://indianrobostore.com","x":400,"y":-3250,"width":480,"height":910,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"ai-compute","type":"text","text":"## AI Compute — NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| AI Performance | 67 TOPS (INT8) |\n| GPU | 1024 CUDA + 32 Tensor cores |\n| CPU | 6-core Arm Cortex-A78AE |\n| Memory | 8GB LPDDR5 (102 GB/s) |\n| Power | 7-25W |\n| ML Frameworks | TensorRT, PyTorch |\n| Camera Interface | 2× MIPI CSI-2 |\n| **Price** | **₹28,499** |\n| **Source** | Hubtronics |\n\n### AI Pipeline (<200ms total)\n```\nCamera → Frame Capture (33ms)\n→ Preprocess (5ms)\n→ NDVI Calc (2ms)\n→ TensorRT Inference (45ms)\n→ Classification (12ms)\n→ Spray Decision (1ms)\n→ MAVLink CMD (5ms)\n→ PWM → Pump (100ms)\n```\n\n### NDVI Decision Matrix\n| NDVI | Zone | Spray Rate |\n|---|---|---|\n| >0.6 | Healthy | None |\n| 0.4-0.6 | Mild Stress | 50 L/ha |\n| 0.2-0.4 | Moderate | 100 L/ha |\n| 0.1-0.2 | Severe | 150 L/ha |\n| <0.1 | Weed/Bare | 200 L/ha |\n\n### Model: EfficientNet-Lite0\n- Accuracy: 75.1% | Latency: 12ms\n- Size: 5.3MB | Power: 7W\n\n**Source:** Hubtronics — https://hubtronics.in\nNVIDIA India — https://www.nvidia.com/en-in/jetson/","x":2120,"y":-3150,"width":480,"height":1200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# COEP Agricultural Hexacopter — Complete Architecture\n## TIHAN + IIT Hyderabad + COEP Technological University\n\n**Project:** National Reference Standards for Edge-AI Enabled Autonomous Agricultural Drones\n**Target:** TRL-6 | **Duration:** 10 months | **Started:** May 29, 2026\n\n| Parameter   | Target    | Verified Baseline     |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------- |\n| MTOW        | 36-45 kg  | 36 kg (verified)      |\n| Tank        | 16L       | 16L HDPE, belly-mount |\n| Flight Time | 20-25 min | 28 min @ 36kg         |\n| Spray Rate  | 1-5 L/m   | 1.34 L/m effective    |\n| Range       | 10-15 km  | 40+ km telemetry      |\n| Frame       | EFT E616P | ₹52,780 (Robokits)    |\n| Total BOM   | —         | ₹4.8L estimated       |","x":-560,"y":-4160,"width":1400,"height":450,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"drone-silhouette","type":"text","text":"## Hexacopter Layout\n\n```\n                          FRONT\n                           ▲\n                M2(CCW)·····│·····M1(CW)\n                     ·      │      ·\n                      ·     │     ·\n                       ·    │    ·\nM3(CW)················[CENTER]················M6(CCW)\n                       ·    │    ·\n                      ·     │     ·\n                     ·      │      ·\n                M4(CCW)·····│·····M5(CW)\n                           │\n                          REAR\n```\n\n### Dimensions\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wheelbase | 1,644mm (diag) |\n| Arm length | 800mm each |\n| Prop sweep | Ø914mm (36\") |\n| Arms | 6× at 60° |\n| Nozzles | 4× XR11002 |\n| Tank | 16L belly |\n\n### Motor Rotation\n| Motor | Spin | Position |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | CW | Front-right |\n| M2 | CCW | Front-left |\n| M3 | CW | Mid-left |\n| M4 | CCW | Rear-left |\n| M5 | CW | Rear-right |\n| M6 | CCW | Mid-right |\n\n**Source:** EFT E616P layout — https://uavgarage.com","x":-2600,"y":-5360,"width":480,"height":1060,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"gps","type":"text","text":"## GPS — v2: HGLRC M100-5883 (1×) or Holybro M9N (1×)\n\n> **v2 CRITICAL FIX (2026-06-02):** v1 had **2× HGLRC M100 Mini** which has **NO COMPASS** — that breaks ArduPilot position-hold / RTL / auto modes. Replaced with **M100-5883** (QMC5883 compass on-module) or **Holybro M9N** (IST8310 compass).\n\n### Budget — HGLRC M100-5883 (1×)\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| GNSS Chip | u-blox M10 |\n| Constellations | GPS+GLONASS+Galileo+BDS (4 concurrent) |\n| Compass | **QMC5883 on-module** ✅ |\n| Update Rate | 10 Hz |\n| Accuracy | 2.0 m CEP |\n| Weight | ~10 g (with compass) |\n| Input | 3.3–5V |\n| **Price** | **₹1,599** |\n| **Source** | FPVMatrix (in stock) |\n\n### Recommended — Holybro M9N (1×)\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| GNSS Chip | u-blox M9N |\n| Compass | **IST8310 on-module** ✅ |\n| Accuracy | 1.5 m CEP |\n| Update Rate | 25 Hz |\n| Weight | 36 g |\n| **Price** | **₹7,525** (Indian Robo Store) / ₹11–15k (UAVGarage) |\n\n### Why single GPS (not dual)\n- ArduPilot EKF needs **GPS + compass together** for blended position\n- A 2nd GPS without compass adds **no redundancy** for compass faults\n- For dual redundancy, use **2× M9N** (₹15k) — overkill for this build\n\n### Mounting Requirements\n- Mast: ≥200 mm above FC (15-20 cm carbon tube, ~₹300)\n- From ESCs: ≥50 mm\n- From VTX: ≥100 mm\n- Antenna upward, calibrate compass after install\n\n**Sources:** FPVMatrix (M100-5883), Indian Robo Store (M9N), Holybro official, hglrc.com","x":400,"y":-2300,"width":480,"height":900,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"telemetry","type":"text","text":"## Communication Systems\n\n### Telemetry — RFD868x (2-radio bundle)\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Frequency | 865-869 MHz (India legal) |\n| Max Power | 1W (30 dBm) |\n| Range | 40+ km LOS |\n| Sensitivity | -121 dBm |\n| Data Rate | 200 kbps |\n| Encryption | AES hardware |\n| Weight | 10g each |\n| **Price** | **₹30,000 (bundle)** |\n| **Source** | GadgetsDeal |\n\n### RC — ELRS 2.4G\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Protocol | CRSF |\n| Frequency | 2.4 GHz |\n| Range | 10+ km |\n| Refresh Rate | up to 1000Hz |\n| Channels | 16 |\n| Weight | 0.5-1.6g |\n| **Price** | **₹1,299-1,999** |\n| **Source** | UAVstore.in |\n\n### Link Budget (10km)\n- EIRP: +32 dBm\n- FSPL: -111.2 dB\n- Received: -71.2 dBm\n- **Margin: +19.8 dB** ✅\n\n### ⚠️ 915 MHz BANNED in India\n### ✅ 865-869 MHz ISM band legal\n\n**Source:** GadgetsDeal — https://gadgetsdeal.in\nUAVstore — https://www.uavstore.in","x":400,"y":-1460,"width":480,"height":1080,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"cost-budget","type":"text","text":"## Budget — v2 BOM (India Prices, June 2026)\n\n> **v2 UPDATE (2026-06-02):** v1 totals **STALE**. v2 corrects: GPS bug (M100 Mini→M100-5883/M9N), battery import landed (₹65k→₹1,06,000), wire gauge 8→6 AWG, +8 mandatory tools, +NPNT/TC budget.\n\n### Path G-A — Recommended (Tattu 30 Ah imported)\n| Category | Cost (₹) | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frame (EFT E616P) | 52,780 | Robokits |\n| Motors (6× X8 class) | 97,500 | IndiaMART |\n| Props (8× MFP 30/36) | 80,000 | IndiaMART |\n| **Battery (1× Tattu 30 Ah Semi-Solid, imported)** | **1,06,000** | Genstattu (USD $1,209 + 18% GST + 30% BCD) |\n| FC (Pixhawk 6C + PM02) | 32,499 | MG Super Labs |\n| **GPS (1× HGLRC M100-5883)** | **1,599** | FPVMatrix (in stock) |\n| Telemetry (RFD868x) | 30,000 | GadgetsDeal |\n| RC (ELRS) | 1,999 | UAVstore |\n| Spray system + tank | 25,000 | IndiaMART |\n| Power distribution (busbar + fuses) | 12,000 | Local |\n| Safety (parachute + strobe) | 15,000 | Local |\n| **Build tools (smoke stopper, balancer, scale, mast, strap, LiPo bag, fuse, 6 AWG wire)** | **7,600** | Generic |\n| Misc (vibration pads, cables, fasteners) | 8,470 | Local |\n| **Grand Total (Path G-A)** | **₹3,70,448** | |\n\n### Path G-B — Budget (2× Tattu 22 Ah Pro, in stock)\n- Same as G-A but battery = 2× Tattu 22 Ah Pro @ ₹45,674 = **₹91,348**\n- 28 kg MTOW (vs 25 kg for G-A), 25 min flight (vs 17.8 min)\n- **Grand Total (Path G-B): ₹3,55,948** (saves ₹14,500, no import lead time)\n\n### Regulatory (NPNT/TC) — separate budget\n| Tier | Cost (₹) | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Minimum (student competition) | **70,000–85,000** | Pilot RPL + 3rd party insurance + UIN |\n| Full commercial | **6,55,000–10,10,000** | + NTH Type Cert (₹4.2L) + RPTO + DGCA fees |\n\n### Total Capex (G-A + minimum regulatory)\n- ₹3,70,448 + ₹85,000 = **₹4,55,448** ✅ fits ₹5L ceiling\n\n**Source:** All prices verified from Indian retailers (Robokits, FPVMatrix, MG Super Labs, Indian Robo Store) and Genstattu (import landed).","x":400,"y":-320,"width":480,"height":1100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"comm-protocols","type":"text","text":"## Communication Protocols\n\n### Protocol Stack\n| Component | Protocol | Speed | Wires |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ESC→FC | DShot600 | 600kbit/s | 1/motor |\n| GPS→FC | UART | 115200 baud | 2+GND |\n| Compass→FC | I2C | 400kHz | 2+GND |\n| IMU→FC | SPI | 50MHz | 4+ |\n| RC Receiver | CRSF | 420kbps | 2+GND |\n| Telemetry | UART MAVLink | 115200 | 2+GND |\n| Jetson→FC | CAN | 1Mbps | 2+GND |\n| Flow Sensor | GPIO IRQ | pulse count | 3 |\n| Pump | PWM | 50Hz | 2 |\n| GCS | MAVLink v2 | radio | wireless |\n\n### Protocol Comparison\n| Protocol | Speed | Bi-dir | Calibration | Use Case |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| PWM | 50Hz | No | Required | Legacy ESCs |\n| DShot | 8kHz | Yes | No | Modern ESCs |\n| CAN | 1Mbit | Yes | No | Industrial |\n| UART | 921kbaud | Yes | N/A | GPS, Telemetry |\n| I2C | 400kHz | Yes | N/A | Sensors |\n| SPI | 50MHz | Yes | N/A | IMU, Baro |\n| CRSF | 250Hz | Yes | No | ELRS |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot protocols — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":400,"y":640,"width":480,"height":880,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"software","type":"text","text":"## Software Stack\n\n### Firmware\n| Tool | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| ArduCopter 4.4 | Flight control |\n| BLHeli_32/AM32 | ESC firmware |\n| JetPack 6.x | Jetson OS + CUDA |\n| TensorRT 8.6+ | AI inference opt |\n\n### Ground Station\n| Tool | Platform |\n|---|---|\n| Mission Planner | Windows |\n| QGroundControl | All platforms |\n\n### AI/ML Pipeline\n| Tool | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| PyTorch | Model training |\n| TensorRT | FP16/INT8 optimization |\n| OpenCV | Computer vision |\n| ROS2 | Middleware (optional) |\n\n### Key ArduPilot Params\n| Prefix | Controls |\n|---|---|\n| ATC_* | Attitude control |\n| MOT_* | Motor mixing |\n| PSC_* | Position control |\n| WP_* | Waypoint navigation |\n| BATT_* | Battery monitoring |\n| FENCE_* | Geofence |\n| FS_* | Failsafe |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot — https://ardupilot.org\nPX4 — https://docs.px4.io\nNVIDIA JetPack — https://developer.nvidia.com/jetpack","x":2120,"y":-720,"width":480,"height":1150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ndvi-camera","type":"text","text":"## NDVI Camera System\n\n### Option: Pi NoIR v3 + Blue Filter\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Resolution | 12MP (4608×2592) |\n| Sensor | Sony IMX477 (NoIR) |\n| Filter | Rosco #2007 Blue |\n| Interface | MIPI CSI-2 |\n| NDVI Formula | (Blue-Red)/(Blue+Red) |\n| Latency | ~33ms/frame |\n| Weight | 45g |\n| **Price** | **₹3,500** |\n\n### Future: MAPIR Survey3W\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Resolution | 12MP RGN |\n| Bands | Red + Green + NIR |\n| NDVI | True (not approx) |\n| **Price** | **~₹33,600 ($400)** |\n| Source | MAPIR direct |\n\n### Overkill: MicaSense RedEdge-P\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Bands | 5 multispectral + RGB |\n| Resolution | 1.6 MP/band |\n| Weight | 363g |\n| **Price** | **₹9,49,000** |\n| Source | XBOOM/Everse |\n\n### NDVI Theory\n```\nNDVI = (NIR - Red) / (NIR + Red)\nRange: -1.0 to +1.0\n\nChlorophyll absorbs Red (660nm)\nMesophyll cells reflect NIR (800nm)\nHealthy = Low Red + High NIR = High NDVI\n```\n\n**Source:** Pi NoIR — https://www.raspberrypi.com\nMAPIR — https://www.mapir.camera\nMicaSense — https://www.micasense.com","x":1600,"y":-2400,"width":480,"height":1250,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"battery","type":"text","text":"## Battery — 3× Tattu 12S 30Ah\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Capacity | 30,000mAh (30Ah) |\n| Config | 12S1P NMC811 Semi-Solid |\n| Nominal Voltage | 44.4V |\n| Energy | 1,332 Wh per pack |\n| Total (3 packs) | 3,996 Wh |\n| Usable (80%DoD×0.88) | 2,813 Wh |\n| C-Rating | 3C cont(90A) / 5C burst(150A) |\n| Weight | 4,900g per pack |\n| Energy Density | 272 Wh/kg |\n| Cycle Life | 500+ (semi-solid) |\n| Connector | AS150U |\n| **Price** | **₹39,680-54,793** |\n| **Source** | Robokits/IndiaMART |\n\n### LiPo Voltage Reference\n| Cell | 100% | Nom | Store | Warn | Crit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1S | 4.20V | 3.70V | 3.85V | 3.50V | 3.30V |\n| 12S | 50.4V | 44.4V | 46.2V | 42.0V | 39.6V |\n\n**Source:** Robokits India — https://robokits.co.in\nIndiaMART — https://indiamart.com","x":-1000,"y":-3250,"width":480,"height":750,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"lipo-safety","type":"text","text":"## LiPo Safety & Charging\n\n### ⚠️ CRITICAL: 12S 30Ah = 1,332 Wh\n- Fire can reach 600°C\n- Toxic HF gas produced\n- ALWAYS balance charge\n- NEVER leave unattended\n\n### Charger Options\n| Charger | Power | Price | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ToolkitRC M8 | 300W | ₹3,052 | RC Mumbai |\n| ToolkitRC M8P | 600W | ₹4,499 | QuadKart |\n| SkyRC D260 Duo | 260W | ₹8,597 | IndianRoboStore |\n| SkyRC D200 Neo | 800W DC | ₹12,999 | Aerokart |\n\n### 12S Charge Times\n| Charger | Time (0-100%) |\n|---|---|\n| M8 (300W) | ~5h |\n| M8P (600W) | ~2.5h |\n| D200 Neo (800W DC) | ~1.2h |\n\n### Safety Rules\n1. NEVER charge unattended\n2. ALWAYS balance charge\n3. NEVER discharge <3.3V/cell\n4. NEVER charge >4.25V/cell\n5. ALWAYS store at 3.85V/cell\n6. ABC extinguisher accessible\n\n**Source:** ToolkitRC — https://www.toolkitrc.com\nSkyRC — https://www.skyrc.com","x":-1000,"y":-1600,"width":480,"height":920,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"source-index","type":"text","text":"## Source Index — Verified References\n\n### Frame & Structure\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| EFT E616P — Robokits India | https://robokits.co.in |\n| EFT E616P — UAVGarage | https://uavgarage.com |\n| EFT E616P — Zbotic | https://zbotic.in |\n\n### Motors & Propulsion\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Hobbywing X9 G2L — IndiaMART | https://indiamart.com |\n| Hobbywing X9 G2L — Zbotic | https://zbotic.in |\n| T-Motor U13 II — MG Super Labs | https://mgsuperlabs.co.in |\n| MAD Motors — Official | https://www.madcomponents.com |\n| Hobbywing MFP 36\" — IndiaMART | https://indiamart.com (Aerorise) |\n\n### Batteries & Power\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Tattu 30Ah — Robokits | https://robokits.co.in |\n| Tattu 30Ah — IndiaMART | https://indiamart.com |\n| Tattu Pro 22Ah — Mavdrones | https://mavdrones.com |\n| GenX 22Ah — Robokits | https://robokits.co.in |\n| AS150 connectors — RC Mumbai | https://rcmumbai.com |\n| Pre-charge design — UWARG | https://uwarg-docs.atlassian.net |\n\n### Flight Electronics\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Pixhawk 6C — Indian Robo Store | https://indianrobostore.com |\n| Pixhawk 6X — MG Super Labs | https://mgsl.in |\n| Cube Orange+ — GadgetsDeal | https://gadgetsdeal.in |\n| HGLRC M10 GPS — Banggood | https://banggood.in |\n| RFD868x — GadgetsDeal | https://gadgetsdeal.in |\n| ELRS receivers — UAVstore | https://www.uavstore.in |\n| FrSky R-XSR — ElectronicsComp | https://electronicscomp.com |\n\n### AI & Sensors\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Jetson Orin Nano — Hubtronics | https://hubtronics.in |\n| Jetson Orin Nano — Robocraze | https://robocraze.com |\n| MicaSense RedEdge-P — XBOOM | https://www.xboom.in |\n| MAPIR Survey3W — MAPIR Direct | https://www.mapir.camera |\n\n### Spray System\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| SHURflo 8000 — Pentair Official | https://www.pentair.com |\n| TeeJet XR11002 — Chemical Containers | https://www.chemicalcontainers.com |\n| YF-S402 — IndiaMART | https://indiamart.com |\n\n### Regulatory (India)\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| DGCA Digital Sky | https://digitalsky.dgca.gov.in |\n| Drone Rules 2021 | https://civillineaviation.gov.in |\n| Drone Rules India 2026 Guide | https://dronevex.in |\n| RPL Training — IID | https://indianinstituteofdrones.com |\n\n### India Market & Schemes\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| PIB — 38575 drones registered | https://static.pib.gov.in |\n| Times of India — Drone stats | https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com |\n| Kisan Drone Yojana | https://agrimachinery.nic.in |\n| Namo Drone Didi — PIB | https://static.pib.gov.in |\n| PLI Scheme — MoCA | https://www.civilaviation.gov.in |\n\n### Competitive Products\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| DJI Agras T25 — Official | https://ag.dji.com/t25/specs |\n| DJI Agras T50 — Official | https://ag.dji.com/t50/specs |\n| DJI Mavic 3M — Official | https://ag.dji.com/mavic-3-m/specs |\n| Marut AG-365S — Official | https://marutdrones.com |\n| Garuda Kisan — Official | https://www.garudaaerospace.com |\n| insideFPV Krishi — Official | https://insidefpv.com |\n| XAG P40 — Official | https://xa.com/en/p40/p40specs |\n| Hylio AG-272 — AgDroneDir | https://agdronedirectory.com |\n\n### TiHAN IIT Hyderabad\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| TiHAN Official | https://tihan.iith.ac.in |\n| NABL eVTOL Lab | https://www.indiandefensenews.in |\n| Palyanka Air Taxi | https://telanganatoday.com |\n\n### Academic & Technical\n| Source | URL |\n|---|---|\n| ArduPilot Documentation | https://ardupilot.org/copter |\n| PX4 Documentation | https://docs.px4.io |\n| Awesome Spectral Indices | https://github.com/davemlz/awesome-spectral-indices |\n| USGS NDVI | https://www.usgs.gov/landsat-missions |\n| ICAR Spray Recommendations | https://icar.org.in |","x":-780,"y":5100,"width":1000,"height":2900,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"motors","type":"text","text":"## Motors — Hobbywing X9 G2L × 6\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| KV Rating | 110 KV |\n| Max Thrust | 24 kg/motor |\n| Combo Weight | 1,532g |\n| Voltage | 12S-14S (18-63V) |\n| Rated Power | 1,600W |\n| Stator | 96×16mm |\n| IP Rating | IPX6 |\n| **Price** | **₹16,250-18,519** |\n| **Source** | IndiaMART/Zbotic |\n\n### Load Table (12S)\n| Thrust | Current | Power | RPM |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4.35 kg | 7.8A | 376W | 1637 |\n| 7.55 kg | 16.6A | 797W | 2153 |\n| 12.0 kg | 32.7A | 1570W | 2725 |\n| 15.9 kg | 49.5A | 2377W | 3148 |\n| 19.9 kg | 70.9A | 3405W | 3570 |\n| 24.0 kg | 95.9A | 4607W | 4000 |\n\n### Hover Current\n| MTOW | Per Motor | Total 6× |\n|---|---|---|\n| 36 kg | 11.9A | 71.4A |\n| 45 kg | 16.5A | 99.0A |\n\n**Source:** IndiaMART — https://indiamart.com\nZbotic — https://zbotic.in","x":-2600,"y":-2420,"width":480,"height":920,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"props","type":"text","text":"## Propellers — Hobbywing MFP 36×11\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Diameter | 36\" (914mm) |\n| Pitch | 11\" |\n| Material | Carbon-Nylon (40% CF) |\n| Blades | 2 (folding, 3-section) |\n| Weight | 287g per prop |\n| Max Thrust | 25 kg |\n| RPM Range | 1,600-3,100 |\n| **Price** | **₹10,000/piece** |\n| **Source** | IndiaMART (Aerorise) |\n\n### KV-Prop Matching\n- 110KV + 36\" = Heavy-lift efficiency\n- High torque, low RPM\n- Folding reduces transport 60%\n\n**Source:** IndiaMART (Aerorise) — https://indiamart.com","x":-2600,"y":-1440,"width":480,"height":600,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"vibration","type":"text","text":"## Vibration Damping\n\n### VIBE Thresholds (ArduPilot)\n| Value (m/s²) | Status | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| <15 | Excellent | None |\n| 15-30 | Good | Monitor |\n| 30-60 | Warning | Investigate |\n| >60 | Critical | Ground |\n\n### Vibration Sources\n1. Prop imbalance (most common)\n2. Motor bearing wear\n3. Arm resonance (32Hz risk)\n4. Loose components\n\n### Solutions\n- Balance all props (magnetic balancer)\n- Motor bearings every 20 flights\n- Silicone grommet FC mount\n- Dynamic notch filters (ArduPilot)\n- RPM filtering (bidirectional DShot)\n- **Upgrade to 30mm arms (48Hz)**\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot VIBE — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":-2600,"y":240,"width":480,"height":740,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"motor-layout","type":"text","text":"## Motor Mixing & Rotation\n\n```\n        Front\n         ▲\n   M2(CCW)  M1(CW)\n        \\  /\n         \\/\n         /\\\n  M3(CW)    M6(CCW)\n        \\  /\n         \\/\n         /\\\n   M4(CCW)  M5(CW)\n         │\n        Rear\n```\n\n### Control Moments\n- **Roll**: M1+M3+M5 vs M2+M4+M6\n- **Pitch**: M1+M2 vs M4+M5\n- **Yaw**: CW motors vs CCW motors\n\n### Single Motor Failure (SMF)\n1. Motor opposite throttled 40%\n2. Remaining 4 motors compensate\n3. FC recalculates thrust budget\n4. Auto landing initiated\n\n### ArduPilot Config\n- FRAME_CLASS=6 (Hexa-X)\n- MOT_PWM_MIN=1000\n- MOT_PWM_MAX=2000\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot motor mix — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":-2600,"y":-760,"width":480,"height":880,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"emergency","type":"text","text":"## Emergency Response\n\n### Crash Response\n1. DO NOT approach if battery damaged\n2. Wait 5 minutes\n3. Check for fire → ABC extinguisher\n4. Photograph scene\n5. Report to DGCA\n\n### Battery Fire\n- NEVER use water on LiPo\n- Use ABC extinguisher or sand\n- Evacuate 30m radius\n- Toxic HF gas → upwind\n\n### Flyaway Protocol\n1. Switch to Stabilize\n2. Reduce throttle\n3. Activate RTL\n4. If no response: cut motors\n5. Geo-fence breach → auto-land\n\n### Emergency Contacts\n| Contact | Number |\n|---|---|\n| DGCA | 011-24610839 |\n| Police | 100 |\n| Fire | 101 |\n| Ambulance | 108 |\n| COEP Lead | [Fill] |\n| TiHAN | 8331040452 |\n\n**Source:** DGCA emergency — https://digitalsky.dgca.gov.in","x":-2360,"y":2370,"width":480,"height":1070,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"thrust-analysis","type":"text","text":"## Thrust-to-Weight Analysis\n\n### Normal Operation (6 motors)\n| Config | Thrust | MTOW | TWR | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 36 kg | 120 kg | 36 kg | **3.33** | ✅ |\n| 39.2 kg | 120 kg | 39.2 kg | **3.06** | ✅ |\n| 45 kg | 120 kg | 45 kg | **2.67** | ✅ |\n| 50 kg | 120 kg | 50 kg | **2.40** | ⚠️ |\n\n### Single Motor Failure (SMF)\n| Config | Avail | MTOW | SMF TWR | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 36 kg | 88 kg | 36 kg | **2.44** | ✅ |\n| 39.2 kg | 88 kg | 39.2 kg | **2.24** | ✅ |\n| 45 kg | 88 kg | 45 kg | **1.96** | ⚠️ |\n\n### Hover Endurance\n| Config | Pure Hover | Mission (20% res) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 36 kg | **47.2 min** | **28.1 min** |\n| 39.2 kg | **42.0 min** | **24.4 min** |\n| 45 kg | **34.6 min** | **17.5 min** |\n\n**Selected: 36 kg config** (best SMF margin + endurance)\n\n**Source:** Hobbywing X9 datasheet — https://zbotic.in\nEFT E616P specs — https://robokits.co.in","x":-2600,"y":-4240,"width":480,"height":840,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"troubleshooting","type":"text","text":"## Troubleshooting Quick Reference\n\n| # | Problem | Cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Won't arm | Pre-arm fail | Check MP messages |\n| 2 | Won't lift | Motor/prop | Check directions |\n| 3 | Oscillating | PID too high | Reduce P 20% |\n| 4 | Drifting | Compass/GPS | Recalibrate |\n| 5 | Motor wrong dir | Wiring/ESC | Swap 2 wires |\n| 6 | Telemetry loss | UART config | Check baud |\n| 7 | Battery sag | Health | Charge, check C |\n| 8 | Vibration | Props | Balance, check motors |\n| 9 | Failsafe triggers | Signal loss | Check link quality |\n| 10 | Flyaway | Compass | Emergency stop |\n| 11 | Motor overheating | Props too large | Smaller props |\n| 12 | CAN bus errors | Wiring | Check 120Ω |\n| 13 | Log clipping | Vibration | Balance props |\n| 14 | High HDOP | GPS view | Open area |\n\n### Emergency Stop Sequence\n1. Switch to Stabilize → throttle down\n2. Turn off TX → triggers failsafe\n3. Press safety switch → motors stop\n4. Last resort: cover props\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot troubleshooting — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":1360,"y":2680,"width":480,"height":880,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"competitive2","type":"text","text":"## Why Build, Not Buy?\n\n1. **Research value** — TRL-6 certification framework\n2. **Cost** — 50% cheaper than DJI\n3. **Customization** — Crop-specific AI models\n4. **Knowledge** — Full system understanding\n5. **India IP** — Own the technology\n6. **Scalability** — Can build fleet\n\n### What DJI Gives You\n- Pre-certified (no NPNT hassle)\n- Plug-and-play\n- 7-12 ha/hr coverage\n- Support network\n\n### What Building Gives You\n- ₹5.2L vs ₹14.15L (T25)\n- 16L tank vs 20L (close)\n- 28 min vs 12 min (better)\n- Custom AI (unlimited potential)\n- Certification framework IP\n\n### Market Opportunity\n- India: 38,575 registered drones\n- 39,890 certified pilots\n- 244 approved training orgs\n- ₹57 Bn market (2024)\n- ₹123 Bn projected (2029)\n- 500+ drone startups\n\n**Source:** Market data — PIB, Times of India (see Source Index)","x":6040,"y":-1650,"width":500,"height":850,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"competitive","type":"text","text":"## Competitive Analysis — Build vs Buy\n\n### Our Custom Build\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Cost | ₹5.2L |\n| Tank | 16L |\n| Flight Time | 28 min |\n| AI | Custom (Jetson) |\n| Certification | EAADC framework |\n| Support | Self |\n\n### Marut AG-365S (Indian)\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Price | ₹6,50,000 |\n| Tank | 10L |\n| Flight Time | 22 min |\n| DGCA | ✅ First certified |\n| Support | Hyderabad |\n\n### insideFPV Krishi (Indian)\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Price | ₹2,50,000 |\n| Tank | 10L |\n| Flight Time | 15-28 min |\n| Frame | 1,648mm wheelbase |\n| Support | India |\n\n### Garuda Kisan 8L\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Price | ₹4,25,000 |\n| Tank | 8L |\n| Flight Time | 7-10 min |\n| Support | Pan-India |\n\n### DJI Agras T25\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Price | ₹14,15,000 |\n| Tank | 20L |\n| Flight Time | 9-12 min |\n| Coverage | 12 ha/hr |\n| Support | DJI India |\n\n**Source:** DJI — https://ag.dji.com\nMarut — https://marutdrones.com\nGaruda — https://www.garudaaerospace.com\ninsideFPV — https://insidefpv.com","x":6040,"y":-3250,"width":500,"height":1480,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"india-ecosystem","type":"text","text":"## India Drone Ecosystem\n\n### Market Stats (2025-2026)\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Registered drones | 38,575 |\n| Certified pilots | 39,890 |\n| Approved RPTOs | 244 |\n| Drone startups | 500+ |\n| Market (2025) | ₹57 Bn |\n| Market (2030 proj) | ₹123 Bn |\n| CAGR | 8.5-24.4% |\n| TC holders | 122 |\n\n### Government Schemes\n| Scheme | Subsidy |\n|---|---|\n| Kisan Drone | 40-100% |\n| Namo Drone Didi | 80% up to ₹8L |\n| PLI 2.0 | ₹1,500 Cr outlay |\n| AIF | 3% subvention |\n\n### TiHAN IIT Hyderabad\n- DST-funded tech hub\n- NABL-accredited eVTOL lab\n- 150kg payload drones (Chakravuyh)\n- 200kg air taxi (Palyanka)\n- Autonomous nav testbed\n- **Contact:** dronetest@tihaniith.in\n\n**Source:** PIB — https://static.pib.gov.in\nTimes of India — https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com\nTiHAN — https://tihan.iith.ac.in","x":6040,"y":-650,"width":500,"height":1015,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"field-ops","type":"text","text":"## Field Operations Protocol\n\n### Pre-Mission (Day Before)\n- [ ] Weather forecast (wind<5m/s)\n- [ ] Battery charged (all packs)\n- [ ] Chemical mixed in tank\n- [ ] Generator fueled\n- [ ] Flight plan uploaded\n- [ ] Area scouted for obstacles\n\n### Mission Day Setup (2h before)\n1. Unload equipment\n2. Set up ground station\n3. Assemble drone (arms, props)\n4. Smoke stopper check\n5. GPS lock (10+ sats, HDOP<2.0)\n6. Compass calibration (if moved >50km)\n7. Upload mission waypoints\n8. Radio link test\n\n### Flight Operations\n```\n1. Arm → Takeoff → Loiter (10m)\n2. Verify systems (10s)\n3. Switch to Auto\n4. Monitor GCS\n5. Mission complete → RTL\n6. Land → Disarm → Safety\n7. Swap battery → Repeat\n```\n\n### Ground Station Equipment\n| Item | Price |\n|---|---|\n| Laptop i5/16GB | ₹55,000 |\n| Generator Honda EU2200i | ₹85,000 |\n| Charger (M8P) | ₹4,499 |\n| Field Box Pelican | ₹12,000 |\n| **GS Total** | **₹1,56,499** |\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot flight modes — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":3800,"y":280,"width":480,"height":1140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"weather","type":"text","text":"## Weather & Environmental Ops\n\n### Wind Impact on Spray\n| Wind Speed | Drift | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0-2 m/s | Minimal | Full spray |\n| 2-5 m/s | Moderate | Reduce 20% |\n| 5-8 m/s | High | No spray |\n| >8 m/s | Severe | Ground all |\n\n### Temperature Effects\n| Temp | Battery | Motor |\n|---|---|---|\n| <0°C | -20% capacity | Normal |\n| 15-35°C | Nominal | Normal |\n| >45°C | Risk thermal | Overheat |\n\n### Altitude & Air Density\n| Altitude | Density | Thrust Loss |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0-500m | 1.225 kg/m³ | 0% |\n| 500-1000m | 1.167 | -5% |\n| >1000m | <1.112 | -9%+ |\n\n### Pune/Deccan Plateau\n- Elevation: ~560m ASL\n- Air density: ~1.17 kg/m³\n- **Thrust loss: ~5% (negligible)**\n\n### Monsoon\n- June-Sep: No outdoor ops\n- Oct-May: Prime season\n\n**Source:** ICAR weather — https://mausam.imd.gov.in","x":3800,"y":-960,"width":480,"height":1000,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"crop-config","type":"text","text":"## Crop-Specific Configurations\n\n### Spray Rates (ICAR Data)\n| Crop | Ground (L/ha) | Drone (L/ha) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rice (paddy) | 200-500 | 15-25 |\n| Wheat | 150-250 | 12-18 |\n| Cotton | 200-500 | 20-25 |\n| Soybean | 200-300 | 15-25 |\n| Grape | 500-1000 | 30-50 |\n| Tomato | 500-750 | 25-40 |\n\n### Pesticide Prices (India)\n| Chemical | Price/L | Dose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Chlorpyrifos 20EC | ₹500-700 | 500-750 ml/acre |\n| Cypermethrin 10EC | ₹400-600 | 200-300 ml/acre |\n| Mancozeb 75WP | ₹350-550/kg | 2-2.5 kg/ha |\n| 2,4-D Amine | ₹300-500/L | 500-750 ml/ha |\n\n### Tank Capacity vs Field\n| Tank | Area/Tank | Tanks/Ha |\n|---|---|---|\n| 16L @ 20 L/ha drone | 0.8 ha | 1.25 |\n| 16L @ 25 L/ha drone | 0.64 ha | 1.56 |\n\n### Nozzle Variants\n| Nozzle | Droplet | Best For |\n|---|---|---|\n| XR11001 | 180µm fine | Fungicide |\n| XR11002 | 220µm med | Insecticide |\n| XR11003 | 280µm coarse | Herbicide |\n\n**Source:** ICAR — https://icar.org.in\nMoA&FW SOP 2023","x":3840,"y":-2160,"width":480,"height":1080,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"spray-system","type":"text","text":"## Spray System\n\n### Fluid Path\n```\n16L HDPE Tank (4 baffles)\n→ 80-mesh Inlet Filter (180µm)\n→ SHURflo 8000 Diaphragm Pump\n  (6.8L/min, 10 bar, 12V DC)\n→ YF-S402 Flow Sensor\n  (1-5 L/min, ±2%)\n→ Pressure Gauge (0-6 bar)\n→ 4-Way Brass Manifold\n→ 4× TeeJet XR11002 Nozzles\n  (0.79 L/min each @ 2 bar)\n← Bypass Return to Tank\n← Pressure Relief Valve (4 bar)\n```\n\n### Component Prices\n| Component | Price | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHURflo 8000 pump | ₹12,000-18,000 | Import |\n| TeeJet XR11002 | ₹500-900 each | IndiaMART |\n| YF-S402 sensor | ₹250-400 | IndiaMART |\n| **Spray System Total** | **~₹25,000** | |\n\n### Performance\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Pump Max | 6.8 L/min |\n| Nozzle Demand (×4) | 3.16 L/min |\n| Mission Effective | ~1.34 L/min |\n| Swath Width | 2.0 m |\n| Droplet VMD | 220µm (medium) |\n| App Rate | 200-300 L/ha |\n\n**Source:** Pentair SHURflo — https://www.pentair.com\nTeeJet — https://www.teejet.com\nYF-S402 — IndiaMART","x":3840,"y":-3400,"width":480,"height":1090,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"alt-fc","type":"text","text":"## Alternative Flight Controllers\n\n### Pixhawk 6X\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Processor | STM32H753 |\n| IMU | Triple redundant |\n| Baro | 2× BMP388 |\n| Price | ₹15,999-36,599 |\n| Source | MG Super Labs |\n\n### Cube Orange+\n| Param | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Processor | STM32H757 dual-core |\n| IMU | Triple (2 isolated) |\n| Baro | 2× MS5611 |\n| Price | ₹22,600-33,499 |\n| Source | GadgetsDeal |\n| Note | Needs carrier board |\n\n### Decision Tree\n```\nBudget < ₹30K → Pixhawk 6C\nBudget ₹30-40K → Pixhawk 6X\nBudget > ₹40K → Cube Orange+\nMust-have triple → Cube Orange+\nResearch focus → Cube Orange+\n```\n\n### Verdict\n- **6C (selected)**: Best value, proven\n- **6X**: Marginal upgrade\n- **Cube**: Overkill unless certifying\n\n**Source:** MG Super Labs — https://mgsl.in\nGadgetsDeal — https://gadgetsdeal.in","x":-4380,"y":520,"width":740,"height":1100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"regulatory","type":"text","text":"## DGCA Regulatory Compliance\n\n### Drone Category: **Small** (2-25kg)\n\n### Requirements\n| Item | Detail | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| Registration | Digital Sky Platform | ₹100 |\n| UIN | Displayed on airframe | — |\n| RPL | 5-7 day training | ₹50,000-75,000 |\n| Insurance | ₹30L coverage | ~₹5,000/yr |\n| NPNT | 865-867MHz module | ₹30,000 |\n| Type Cert | QCI agency | ₹2-5L |\n\n### Airspace Zones\n- 🟢 Green: Unrestricted, NPNT auto\n- 🟡 Yellow: Controlled, ATC permission\n- 🔴 Red: Prohibited\n\n### Penalties\n- Flying without reg: up to ₹1L\n- NPNT violation: up to ₹1L\n- Endangering safety: up to ₹5L\n\n### Required Docs\n- DGCA registration + UIN\n- Type Certificate (QCI agency)\n- RPL (10yr validity)\n- Insurance certificate\n- NPNT module cert\n- Flight log records (30d min)\n\n### ⚠️ 915 MHz telemetry BANNED\n### ✅ 865-867 MHz ISM band legal\n\n**Source:** DGCA Digital Sky — https://digitalsky.dgca.gov.in\nDrone Rules 2021","x":-560,"y":1960,"width":480,"height":980,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"timeline","type":"text","text":"## Project Execution Timeline\n\n### 6 Phases (10 months)\n| Phase | Months | Key Deliverable |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Foundation | 1-2 | Standards Gap Analysis |\n| 2. Testbed | 2-4 | 36kg flight testbed |\n| 3. Edge-AI | 4-6 | AI spray system |\n| 4. Compliance | 5-7 | Certification framework |\n| 5. Validation | 7-9 | TRL-6 validation |\n| 6. Handover | 9-10 | Report + GitHub |\n\n### Success Criteria (TRL-6)\n- Autonomous GPS waypoint flight\n- AI inference <200ms/frame\n- Variable-rate spray proven\n- Complete audit trail logged\n- Safety mode on camera failure\n- Certification framework draft\n\n### Risk Mitigation\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| AI accuracy <95% | Rule-based fallback |\n| Flight time <20min | Reduce spray, more battery |\n| DGCA delays | Research first, submit after |\n| Hardware failure | Spare components on hand |\n\n**Source:** Project plan — COEP/IIT Hyderabad","x":-560,"y":3020,"width":480,"height":840,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"testing","type":"text","text":"## Testing Protocol — 7 Gates\n\n| Gate | Name | Duration | Pass Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G0 | Bench Test | 1-2d | Thrust≥80%, vib<0.5g |\n| G1 | Ground Sweep | 0.5d | VIB<30, ESC<80°C |\n| G2 | Tethered Hover | 1d | Drift<0.5m, alt±0.3m |\n| G3 | Free Hover | 1-2d | Endurance≥10min |\n| G4 | Flight Envelope | 2-3d | Alt≥20m, speed≥10m/s |\n| G5 | Spray Integration | 1-2d | Flow±10%, cutoff<2s |\n| G6 | Mission Validation | 1-2d | 100% waypoints |\n\n**Total: 14-17 days**\n\n### Pre-Flight Checklist\n- [ ] Battery charged, no swelling\n- [ ] Props tight, correct CW/CCW\n- [ ] GPS lock (10+ sats, HDOP<2.0)\n- [ ] Radio connected, failsafe tested\n- [ ] Frame tight, no loose wires\n- [ ] Area clear, weather OK\n- [ ] Fire extinguisher accessible\n\n**Source:** ArduPilot testing — https://ardupilot.org/copter","x":-560,"y":3960,"width":480,"height":800,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"grp-cam-payload","type":"group","x":-4460,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"2","label":"Camera Payload (Tier A+B)"},
		{"id":"grp-datasets","type":"group","x":-2900,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"3","label":"Datasets & Annotation"},
		{"id":"grp-ml-models","type":"group","x":-1300,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"4","label":"ML Models"},
		{"id":"grp-edge","type":"group","x":300,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"5","label":"Edge Deployment (Jetson)"},
		{"id":"grp-cloud-gis","type":"group","x":1900,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"6","label":"Cloud + GIS"},
		{"id":"grp-india-reg","type":"group","x":3500,"y":8100,"width":1500,"height":2900,"color":"1","label":"Indian Context & Compliance"},
		{"id":"cam-rededge","type":"text","text":"## MicaSense RedEdge-P\n**5-band Multispectral**\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Bands | B/G/R/RE/NIR + pan |\n| Res | 1456x1088/band |\n| Weight | 350g |\n| Power | 7-10W |\n| Interface | USB2/Eth/GPIO |\n| GSD @10m | 6.4 mm/px |\n| **Price** | **Rs 8.5-9.5L** |\n\n**Use:** NDVI/NDRE gold standard\n\n**Caveat:** Post-flight only, no real-time stream\n\n**Source:** aeromotus.com — https://www.aeromotus.com/product/rededge-p/","x":-4360,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cam-oakd","type":"text","text":"## Luxonis OAK-D Pro\n**Stereo AI Camera (4 TOPS VPU)**\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| RGB | 4K (3840x2160) |\n| Stereo | 2x 640x480 GS |\n| AI chip | Myriad X (4 TOPS) |\n| Depth | 0.2-10m |\n| Weight | 80g |\n| Power | 3-5W |\n| **Price** | **Rs 53,399** |\n\n**Use:** On-camera YOLO inference, real-time spot spray\n\n**Source:** MG Super Labs — https://www.mgsuperlabs.co.in/estore/OAK-D-Pro-Auto-Focus","x":-4360,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cam-imx477","type":"text","text":"## 2x Arducam IMX477 + Filters\n**DIY NDVI verification rig**\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Sensor | Sony IMX477 12.3MP |\n| Filters | 650nm R + 850nm NIR |\n| Weight | 120g (both) |\n| Power | 2.6W |\n| Interface | MIPI CSI-2 |\n| **Price** | **~Rs 31,000** |\n\n**NDVI:** (NIR-R)/(NIR+R)\n\n**Source:** robu.in + midopt.com","x":-4360,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cam-tierb","type":"text","text":"## Sony A7R IV + FLIR Lepton 3.5\n**RGB Mapping + Thermal**\n\n| Item | Spec | Price |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sony A7R IV | 61MP full-frame | Rs 2,40,990 |\n| + Gremsy T3 gimbal | 3-axis | ~Rs 40K |\n| FLIR Lepton 3.5 | 160x120 thermal | Rs 61,030 |\n| PureThermal USB | UVC adapter | included |\n| **Combined** | | **~Rs 3.5L** |\n\n**Use:** Spray verification + disease hotspot\n\n**Source:** sony.co.in, tanotis.com","x":-4360,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"data-global","type":"text","text":"## Global Datasets (Mix Indian+Global)\n\n| Dataset | Size | License | Use |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PlantVillage | 54K imgs, 38 cls | CC-BY 4.0 | Disease baseline |\n| DeepWeeds | 17K, 8 weeds | CC-BY 4.0 | Weed det |\n| CottonWeedDet12 | 5K, 12 cls | CC-BY | Cotton weed |\n| AgriVision | UAV, 9 cls | Research | Crop seg |\n| VisDrone | 10K drone | CC-BY-NC-SA | General det |\n| WeedSense 2025 | Multi-modal | CC-BY | SOTA bench |\n\n**Source:** Hughes 2016, Olsen 2019 — https://www.mdpi.com/1424-8220/19/11/2536","x":-2800,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"data-india","type":"text","text":"## Indian Datasets & Sources\n\n| Resource | Use |\n|---|---|\n| **ICAR** (icar.org.in) | Crop varieties |\n| **ICRISAT Hyd** | Dryland crops |\n| **ICAR-NBSS&LUP** | Soil maps |\n| **PMFBY** | Crop cutting GT |\n| **Bhuvan ISRO** | Satellite imagery |\n| **10K India Fields** (Zenodo) | Field boundaries |\n| **IMD Mausam** | Weather |\n| **Fields of the World** | Sentinel-2 + fields |\n\n**All free. Bhuvan + ICAR = killer Indian GT stack**\n\n**Source:** bhuvan.nrsc.gov.in, icrisat.org","x":-2800,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"data-annotate","type":"text","text":"## Annotation Stack\n\n**CVAT** (self-host on COEP VM)\n- Free, MIT, full features\n- Video + polygons + SAM\n- Export COCO/YOLO\n\n**SAM2 auto-label** (Apache-2.0)\n- Bootstrap ~70% polygons\n- Human verify 30%\n\n**FiftyOne** (Apache-2.0)\n- Error analysis / viz\n- Companion tool\n\n**Roboflow Research**\n- Free 10K+50K images (.edu)\n- Public data only\n\n**Source:** github.com/cvat-ai","x":-2800,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"data-inhouse","type":"text","text":"## In-House Collection Plan\n**GAP: No public Indian ag drone dataset at scale**\n\n**Maharashtra target crops:**\n- Cotton (Kharif Aug-Sep)\n- Soybean (Kharif Aug)\n- Sugarcane (Rabi Dec-Feb)\n- Wheat (Rabi Dec)\n- Chickpea (Rabi Feb)\n\n**Spec per class:**\n- 500-1000 imgs/weed class\n- 4 growth stages x 2 seasons\n- 5 sites (Pune/Ahmednagar)\n- Agronomist GT (ICAR)\n\n**License:** Mendeley CC-BY 4.0","x":-2800,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"model-yolo","type":"text","text":"## YOLOv11n — Real-Time Weed\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Year | 2024/9 (Ultralytics) |\n| Params | 2.6M |\n| COCO mAP | 39.5 |\n| Orin Nano FPS | ~125 (FP16 TRT) |\n| End-to-end | ~50-70 FPS |\n| License | AGPL-3.0 |\n\n**YOLOv9-GELAN** = more accurate (0.935 mAP, weed 2024) but ~70 FPS\n\n**Deploy:** `yolo export format=engine half=True`\n\n**Source:** docs.ultralytics.com — https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolo11","x":-1200,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"model-seg","type":"text","text":"## U-Net + EfficientNet-B0\n**Crop Row / Weed Boundary**\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Architecture | U-Net decoder |\n| Backbone | EfficientNet-B0 |\n| Params | 5.1M |\n| mIoU (CoFly weed) | **56.21%** (Shahi 2024) |\n| F1 (CoFly weed) | **88.24%** |\n| Orin Nano FPS | ~15 (est) |\n| License | MIT |\n\n**Best published weed seg model**\n\n**Source:** Shahi et al. 2024 — https://acquire.cqu.edu.au/articles/journal_contribution/26401549","x":-1200,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"model-cls","type":"text","text":"## EfficientNet-B0 — Disease\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Year | 2019 (Google) |\n| Params | 5.3M |\n| ImageNet Top-1 | 77.1% |\n| Orin Nano FPS | ~150 (FP16 TRT) |\n| License | Apache-2.0 |\n\n**Use:** Train on PlantVillage (54K imgs, CC-BY)\n\n**Pretrain alternatives:**\n- DINOv2-S (21M, SSL) — ag SOTA 2025\n- Prithvi-EO-2.0 (600M, 6-band)\n\n**Source:** lukas/efficientdet — https://github.com/lukas/efficientdet","x":-1200,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"model-found","type":"text","text":"## Foundation Models (Edge-Feasible)\n\n| Model | Params | FPS (Nano) | License |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Florence-2-base** | 230M | ~1-2 (INT4) | MIT |\n| GroundingDINO-T | 170M | ~5-8 | Apache-2.0 |\n| **DINOv2-S** | 21M | ~50 | Apache-2.0 |\n| MobileSAM | 10.1M | ~5-10 | Apache-2.0 |\n| DINOv2-B | 86M | ~25 | Apache-2.0 |\n\n**Use:** Zero-shot rare species, text-prompted detection\n\n**Only Florence-2-base fits 8GB comfortably**\n\n**Source:** HuggingFace + Jetson AI Lab","x":-1200,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"edge-jetson","type":"text","text":"## Jetson Orin Nano 8GB Super\n**Edge AI Compute**\n\n| Spec | Value |\n|---|---|\n| GPU | 1024-core Ampere |\n| CPU | **6-core** A78AE |\n| AI (Super) | 67 sparse / 34 dense INT8 |\n| RAM | 8GB LPDDR5, 102 GB/s |\n| Power | 7W/15W/**25W** MAXN_SUPER |\n| JetPack | 6.2 / 6.2.1 (L4T 36.4.4) |\n| **Price** | **~Rs 28K devkit** |\n\n**Lifecycle:** Until 2032\n\n**Source:** NVIDIA devkit — https://developer.nvidia.com/embedded/learn/get-started-jetson-orin-nano-devkit","x":400,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"edge-deepstream","type":"text","text":"## DeepStream 7.1 + TensorRT 10.3\n**Multi-Camera Inference Pipeline**\n\n```\nCSI/USB -> nvstreammux -> nvinfer (YOLOv11n INT8)\n  -> nvtracker (NvDCF) -> nvinfer (EffB0)\n  -> nvdsanalytics (ROI) -> ROS2 publish\n```\n\n**Components:**\n- CUDA 12.6\n- cuDNN 9.3\n- VPI 3.2 (preprocess)\n- TensorRT 10.3 (mandatory)\n\n**FPS:** ~50 single-stream YOLOv11n\n\n**Source:** NVIDIA DeepStream 7.1 — https://docs.nvidia.com/metropolis/deepstream/7.1","x":400,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"edge-ros2","type":"text","text":"## ROS 2 Humble + MAVROS\n**Robot Middleware**\n\n| Layer | Pick |\n|---|---|\n| ROS distro | Humble (LTS, EOL May 2027) |\n| DDS | Cyclone DDS |\n| FC bridge | MAVROS (ArduPilot) |\n| Image transport | Isaac ROS NITROS |\n| GCS | Foxglove Studio |\n| Mission | QGroundControl |\n\n**Jazzy NOT supported on Jetson** (needs Ubuntu 24.04)\n\n**Hot path:** C++ + intra-process, avoid Python\n\n**Source:** nvidia-isaac-ros.github.io","x":400,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"edge-nvenc-warn","type":"text","text":"## NO NVENC on Orin Nano\n**CRITICAL CONSTRAINT**\n\n| Want | Reality |\n|---|---|\n| Hardware H.264/H.265 | NOT present |\n| NVDEC (decode) | 1x 4K60 H.264/H.265 |\n| HW JPEG | via nvjpegenc |\n\n**Workarounds:**\n- Software libx264 (`x264enc speed-preset=ultrafast tune=zerolatency`) eats 1-2 A78AE cores\n- HW MJPEG snapshots (no inter-frame)\n- WebRTC + libx264 = ~1 Mbps / 720p / 15 fps realistic\n\n**Pin libx264 to one core via taskset**\n\n**Source:** NVIDIA forum Dec 2025 — https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/354032","x":400,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cloud-photo","type":"text","text":"## Photogrammetry (Free Stack)\n\n| Tool | License | Rs |\n|---|---|---|\n| **ODM 3.5+** | AGPLv3 | **0** (best for thesis) |\n| WebODM | SaaS | 42/credit |\n| Metashape Std EDU | Proprietary | **5,000** (no MS) |\n| Metashape Pro | Proprietary | 2.94L (one-time) |\n| Pix4Dmapper | Proprietary | 3.35L/yr (overpriced) |\n| DJI Terra Ag | Free w/ T25 | 0 (DJI only) |\n| COLMAP | BSD | 0 (RGB only) |\n| Meshroom | MPL2 | 0 (RGB only) |\n\n**ODM `--multispectral`** gives NDVI in one command\n\n**Source:** opendronemap.org — https://github.com/OpenDroneMap/ODM","x":2000,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cloud-ndvi","type":"text","text":"## NDVI / Vegetation Index Pipeline\n**Custom Python (30 lines)**\n\n```python\nNDVI  = (NIR-RED)/(NIR+RED+1e-6)\nNDRE  = (NIR-RE)/(NIR+RE+1e-6)\nGNDVI = (NIR-GREEN)/(NIR+GREEN+1e-6)\nEVI   = 2.5*(NIR-RED)/(NIR+6*RED-7.5*BLUE+1)\n```\n\n**Stack:**\n- `rasterio` (read GeoTIFF)\n- `numpy` (array math)\n- `GDAL` (reproject)\n- `Orfeo ToolBox` (advanced)\n\n**Source:** atedstone/micasense_calibration — https://github.com/atedstone/micasense_calibration","x":2000,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cloud-qgis","type":"text","text":"## QGIS + Google Earth Engine\n**GIS Stack (all free)**\n\n| Tool | Use |\n|---|---|\n| **QGIS 3.40 LTR** | Local analysis |\n| **Google Earth Engine** | Sentinel-2/Landsat free |\n| Orfeo Toolbox plugin | Pansharpening, seg |\n| SAGA / GRASS plugins | Terrain, geostat |\n| Bhuvan (ISRO) | Indian satellite |\n| Fields of the World | ML field seg |\n\n**Cost:** Rs 0, replicate 90% of ArcGIS Pro\n\n**Source:** qgis.org, earthengine.google.com","x":2000,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cloud-spray-map","type":"text","text":"## Prescription Map Generator\n\n**Pipeline:**\n1. NDVI raster (from cloud-ndvi)\n2. Zonal stats (rasterio + shapefile)\n3. K zones (0-0.2, 0.2-0.4, ...)\n4. Vectorize to Shapefile/GeoJSON\n5. Re-project WGS84\n6. KML for DJI / MAVLink for custom\n\n**Rate table:**\n| NDVI | L/ha | PWM |\n|---|---|---|\n| <0.2 | 100% | Full |\n| 0.2-0.4 | 50-80% | Variable |\n| >0.6 | 0% | Skip |\n\n**Source:** PIX4Dfields zonation — https://support.pix4d.com/hc/en-us/articles/360000899466","x":2000,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ind-dgca","type":"text","text":"## DGCA NPNT Compliance\n**Mandatory for >250g drones**\n\n| Requirement | Cost |\n|---|---|\n| UIN registration | Rs 100 (Digital Sky) |\n| RPL (5-7 day) | Rs 50-75K per pilot |\n| Drone insurance | Rs 5-20K/yr |\n| **NPNT module** | **Rs 30K** (IITB IHUB NTIH) |\n| Airspace map | Free |\n\n**Link:** digitalsky.aai.aero\n\n**For custom Pixhawk build:** integrate open-source NPNT module from IHUB NTIH IITB\n\n**Penalties:** up to Rs 1L for violation\n\n**Source:** DGCA Drone Rules 2021 — https://digitalsky.dgca.gov.in","x":3600,"y":8200,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ind-dpdp","type":"text","text":"## DPDP Act 2023\n**Data Privacy (effective May 2027)**\n\n| Item | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Max penalty | **Rs 250 crore per breach** |\n| Substantive compliance | 13 May 2027 |\n| Data Protection Board | Active Nov 2025 |\n\n**For drone data:**\n- Anonymize farmer identity\n- Strip PII/Aadhaar from EXIF\n- Define retention policy\n- Informed consent in writing\n- Get farmer MOU\n\n**Ag geodata = personal data** if traceable\n\n**Source:** dpdpact2023.com — https://www.hoganlovells.com/en/publications/indias-digital-personal-data-protection-act-2023-brought-into-force-","x":3600,"y":8940,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ind-4g","type":"text","text":"## Rural India 4G/5G\n**Connectivity for data upload**\n\n| Operator | Speed (median) | Villages 4G |\n|---|---|---|\n| Jio | 107.3 Mbps | 88.9% |\n| Airtel | 58.2 Mbps | Premium |\n| Vi | 25.1 Mbps | Declining |\n| BSNL | 9.0 Mbps | Govt rural |\n| 5G | 200+ urban | **Rural patchy** |\n\n**Starlink:** NOT licensed in India 2026\n\n**Realistic:** 5-10 Mbps uplink\n**Plan:** Store-and-forward as default\n\n**Source:** Ookla India 1H 2025 — https://www.ookla.com/articles/india-mobile-connectivity-1h2025","x":3600,"y":9680,"width":480,"height":680,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ind-cdac","type":"text","text":"## Free Indian Compute (CDAC PARAM)\n\n| Resource | GPU | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| PARAM Shakti (IITM) | 30x A100 | **Free** (NSM proposal) |\n| PARAM Pravega (IISc) | 40x V100 | **Free** (NSM proposal) |\n| PARAM Rudra 2025 | New A100/H100 | Free (allocated) |\n\n**Apply via NSM portal** (nsmindia.in)\n- Need COEP faculty PI\n- Project proposal: 2-4 weeks\n- Free = replaces E2E H100 spend (Rs 8K/cycle)\n\n**Also:** E2E Networks TIR (Rs 70/hr H100 spot) — INR debit card OK\n\n**Source:** nsmindia.in, e2enetworks.com","x":3600,"y":10420,"width":480,"height":580,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"v2-verified-calculated","type":"text","text":"## Verified vs Calculated (Transparency Note) — v2 BOM (2026-06-02)\n\n**VERIFIED** — Confirmed from manufacturer datasheet or live Indian retail (June 2026):\n- All component prices, datasheet specs, lead times from web search\n- Tattu 30 Ah Semi-Solid 12S = ₹1,06,000 imported (Genstattu USD $1,209 + 18% GST + 30% BCD)\n- NPNT/TC fees (UIN ₹100, UAOP ₹2.5k, NTH Type Cert ₹4.2L, RPTO ₹50–65k) — from DGCA/PIB Sep 2025\n- Pixhawk 6C + PM02 ₹32,499 (MG Super Labs) / ₹33,899 (Robocraze) — live retail\n- HGLRC M100-5883 ₹1,599 (FPVMatrix, in stock) — live retail\n- Holybro M9N ₹7,525 (Indian Robo Store) — live retail\n- mPower 12S 21 Ah Li-ion ₹50,000 (quote-based) — manufacturer quote\n- 8.4 kg vs 4.9 kg battery weight, 1,332 Wh vs 977 Wh capacity — datasheet\n\n**CALCULATED** — Derived from math, not measured:\n- 17.8 min flight time at 25 kg MTOW — calculated from hover power (3,420 W) and battery capacity (1,332 Wh × 80% DoD)\n- 1.6× thrust margin — calculated from X8 max thrust (15 kg/axis) vs hover load (4.17 kg/axis)\n- MTOW 25 kg = frame (7 kg) + 6× X8 (3 kg) + 10L tank (5.8 kg) + battery (4.9 kg) + Pixhawk 6C (0.05 kg) + 8 PDB/avionics (0.5 kg) + 6 ESC (1.2 kg) + spray system (1.0 kg) + wiring/connectors (0.5 kg) + 1.05 kg margin = 25.0 kg — weight estimate, not measured\n- LCOE ₹187–794/flight-hr — calculated from pack cost / cycles / 267 hr/yr\n- Battery leads 20–30 day import — based on genstattu.com shipping estimates, not actual order\n\n**ESTIMATED** — Generic pricing, not from specific retailer:\n- Smoke stopper ₹1,200, prop balancer ₹800, calibration scale ₹2,500, GPS mast ₹300, battery strap ₹200, LiPo bag ₹800 — generic tool/component prices\n- 6 AWG wire ₹1,200 for 5 m — generic electrical supply pricing\n- AS150 + XT90 connector kit ₹1,500 — generic\n- 2× spare 3011 prop ₹3,500 — based on ₹1,750 per prop generic pricing\n- 17.6/17.8 min flight time — calculation, not actual flight data\n- 0.5–1 acre coverage per 10 L flight — calculated from spray rate (1–5 L/min) × swath (3–5 m) × speed (3–5 m/s), not field-tested","x":-780,"y":8100,"width":1000,"height":1100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"v2-gaps-identified","type":"text","text":"## Gaps Identified (Buildability Audit) — v2 (2026-06-02)\n\nThese items would prevent a working build if not addressed:\n\n### Critical (will break the build)\n\n1. **GPS compass bug (FIXED in v2)** — HGLRC M100 Mini has NO compass; without it ArduPilot position-hold/RTL/auto modes don't work. v2 uses M100-5883 or Holybro M9N. Updated 2026-06-02.\n\n2. **Tattu 30 Ah Semi-Solid 12S not in stock in India** — must import 20-30 days via Genstattu/Foxtech/Motionew. Risk: customs delay. Budget option: 2× Tattu 22 Ah Pro in stock at Robokits (G-B, ₹3,55,948).\n\n3. **No per-cell battery monitoring in flight** — Tattu 30 Ah Semi-Solid has no smart BMS that ArduPilot can read. MAUCH HS-200-LV gives pack voltage + current only. Need a balance lead tap to ADC or DroneCAN battery monitor (TBS Bat-Pro, ~₹5,000–8,000). Not in v2 BOM.\n\n4. **Regulatory: NPNT/Type Certificate** — A custom Pixhawk hexacopter CANNOT legally fly under NPNT without a Type Certificate. For SAE DDC 2026 competition, must confirm with organizers whether the competition site has a blanket exemption. If not, ₹4.2L TC at NTH Ghaziabad required (3-6 month timeline). v2 budgeted ₹70-85k for minimum path.\n\n5. **No ArduPilot parameter file** — 20+ parameters must be set (INS_GYRO_RATE, ATC_RAT_P/I/D, ATC_ANG_P/I/D, COMPASS_*, INS_ACCEL_FILTER, MOT_PWM_MIN/MAX). None of this is in BOM. User has zero ArduPilot/DroneCAN/ag-spray experience. Must read ArduPilot docs and follow tuning guide (~8-12 hours of work).\n\n### Medium (won't break but will surprise)\n\n6. **No actual flight test data** — 17.8 min flight time is calculated math, not measured. Actual flight time will be ±15%.\n\n7. **No CG (center of gravity) verification procedure** — must weigh each component and compute centroid. Mismatched CG = uncontrollable drone.\n\n8. **No compass calibration step-by-step** — required for ArduPilot. Mentioned in build guide but no detailed procedure.\n\n9. **No motor direction verification procedure** — 6 motors, CW/CCW pairing; one wrong direction = flipped crash.\n\n10. **No ground station laptop** — not in BOM. Existing laptop with Mission Planner or new ruggedized (~₹50k).\n\n11. **2× spare props at ₹3,500 may not be enough** — student pilots crash. Should budget 4-6 spares.\n\n12. **vibration analysis capability** — 30\" props must be balanced; without FFT analyzer can't verify clean IMU data.\n\n13. **No tether for first hover test** — recommended for safety, not in BOM.\n\n14. **No NPNT hardware module sourced** — Johnnette U2.0 is quote-based (contact@johnnette.com), not public price, not in stock.\n\n### Low (cosmetic)\n\n15. **G10 vibration pads were ₹1,800 in v1, verified ₹500 in v2** — over-priced in v1, corrected.\n\n16. **2 stale v7 docx files in workspace** — confusing. v9 will replace v8.","x":280,"y":8100,"width":1000,"height":1300,"color":"1"}
	],
